Include <sys/types.h> in the WireGuardKitC umbrella header.

WireGuardKitC.h re-declares struct ctl_info and struct sockaddr_ctl, copied
from <sys/kern_control.h>, using the BSD type names u_int32_t, u_char and
u_int16_t. It never includes the header that defines them.

Under the implicit-modules build this compiled, because by the time the
umbrella header was parsed those names had leaked in from another header in
the same translation unit. Xcode 26 builds Swift with explicit modules, which
precompiles the module map on its own, and there the names are simply
undefined:

    error: declaration of 'u_int32_t' must be imported from module
    '_DarwinFoundation1.unsigned_types.u_int32_t' before it is required

One include fixes it. Reported nowhere upstream that we can push to, so it is
applied here at fetch time; `make upstream` fails loudly if it stops applying,
which is what should happen if the pinned revision ever moves.

--- a/Sources/WireGuardKitC/WireGuardKitC.h
+++ b/Sources/WireGuardKitC/WireGuardKitC.h
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 // Copyright © 2018-2023 WireGuard LLC. All Rights Reserved.
 
+#include <sys/types.h>
+
 #include "key.h"
 #include "x25519.h"
 
